IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`

§ `Chapter 5 -- Abetment`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 107, 108, 108A, 108B.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.

§§ `Section 107 -- Abetment of the doing of a thing`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 107(1)"
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person abets the doing of a thing` IF
        ab's `instigates any person to do the thing`
    OR  (    ab's `engages with one or more other persons in a conspiracy for the doing of the thing`
         AND ab's `an act or illegal omission takes place in pursuance of that conspiracy and in order to the doing of that thing`)
    OR  ab's `intentionally aids by any act or illegal omission the doing of the thing`

-- s 107(2): a person may abet despite facts of which he is unaware which make
-- the doing of the thing impossible. The impossibility flag is not a precondition.

§§ `Section 108 -- Abettor`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 108"
@export Decide whether the person abets an offence under Penal Code 1871 sections 107 and 108
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc Instigation, conspiracy (with an act or illegal omission in pursuance), or intentional aiding. The thing abetted must be an offence or would be an offence if committed by a person capable of committing an offence with the same intention or knowledge as the abettor. Impossibility unknown to the abettor does not prevent abetment (s 107(2)).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person abets an offence` IF
        `the person abets the doing of a thing` ab
    AND ab's `the thing would be an offence if committed by a person capable of committing an offence with the same intention or knowledge as the abettor`

§§ `Section 108A -- Abetment in Singapore of an offence outside Singapore`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 108A"
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person abets an offence outside Singapore from Singapore` IF
        `the person abets an offence` ab
    AND ab's `the abetment takes place in Singapore`
    AND ab's `the act abetted would be committed outside Singapore`
    AND ab's `the thing would be an offence if committed by a person capable of committing an offence with the same intention or knowledge as the abettor`

§§ `Section 108B -- Abetment outside Singapore of an offence in Singapore`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 108B"
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person abets an offence in Singapore from outside Singapore` IF
        `the person abets an offence` ab
    AND ab's `the offence abetted would be committed in Singapore`
    AND ab's `any or all of the acts constituting the abetment were done outside Singapore`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes abetment of an offence` IF
        `the person abets an offence` (a's `abetment`)
    AND NOT (`a general exception applies` a)

